==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Coined by {{w|Francis Galton}} in 1885, from {{suf|en|percent|ile}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|pər-sĕnʹ-tīl}}, {{IPA|en|/pəɹ.ˈsɛn.taɪl/}}
** {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/pɚ.ˈsɛn.taɪl/}}
** {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/pə.ˈsɛn.taɪl/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛntaɪl}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|statistics}} Any of the ninety-nine [[point]]s that divide an [[ordered]] [[distribution]] into one hundred parts, each containing one [[per cent]] of the [[population]].
# {{lb|en|statistics}} Any one of the hundred groups so divided.
#: ''He is highly intelligent – he has an IQ in the top percentile.''

